      "side": 1,
      "message": "Once you\u0027ve created a Zephyr specific `temp_sensor_read()`, you can conditionally compile in the GPIO check, only if at least one temp sensor has a power GPIO.\n\n```\n#if ANY_INST_HAS_POWER_GPIOS\n\t/* Check our power GPIO, if defined */\n\tif (sensor-\u003epower_gpio.port \u0026\u0026 \n\t    !gpio_pin_get_dt(sensor-\u003epower_gpio))\n\t\treturn EC_ERROR_NOT_POWERED;\n#endif\n```\n\nSee the upstream EEPROM driver for an example of this:\n\nhttps://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/99ab33d117a9179a8626139ce9005e899874c9d0/drivers/eeprom/eeprom_at2x.c#L37",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "6ae8786f46faf4b66ac3f53ff69deca8d974b51f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
